# finished_utc=2026-08-10T04:12:29Z

########################################################################
# ANALYSIS  (evidence, not a gate assertion -- no wall-clock number is
# asserted anywhere in the suite)
#
# slope, ms per record of history (least squares over all 800 samples):
#   BEFORE  0.933199  0.953133  1.311153     range 0.933 - 1.311
#   AFTER   0.604023  0.663789  0.301523     range 0.302 - 0.664
#   -> RANGES DO NOT OVERLAP. Every AFTER rep is below every BEFORE rep.
#
# mean latency of the last 50 admissions (history ~750-800), ms:
#   BEFORE   680.40   743.97  1244.14        range 680 - 1244
#   AFTER    547.99   578.74   554.23        range 548 - 579
#   -> RANGES DO NOT OVERLAP.
#
# Note the SPREAD, which is itself a finding: the AFTER arm's steady-state
# latency varies by 5% across reps while the BEFORE arm varies by 83%.
# A quadratic term is what makes a run sensitive to machine state, and the
# arm that lost it also lost most of its variance. The BEFORE r3 and
# AFTER r4 reps ran as load was rising (loadavg 26.9 and after), which is
# where BEFORE's 1.311 and AFTER's odd 0.302-slope/290ms-intercept fit
# come from -- AFTER r4's profile is a step, not a line, so its least
# squares slope understates and its intercept overstates. Its last-50
# mean (554.23) is in family with the other two AFTER reps, which is why
# both statistics are reported rather than only the fit.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SHOW. The slope is REDUCED, not removed.
# Cost still grows with history, because the reconcile still replays the
# conversation four times per commit (docs/design/p0-60-admission-cost.md
# section 1a, pinned by tests_p0_60_admission_cost). What landed is the
# removal of the O(N^2) engine scan inside each of those four passes.
#
# NOT COMPARABLE to the 1.153 ms/record field figure: that was measured
# over TCP with 9,728-byte payloads at 8c8adec; this is in-process with
# 512-byte payloads at 9c22b84 vs this lane's tip. Only BEFORE-vs-AFTER
# within this file is a controlled comparison.
#
# Probe source: a throwaway #[test] added identically to both trees,
# never committed, removed after the run. Release profile both arms.
########################################################################
